<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:InsolDia:1</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>InsolDia</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>Given a digital elevation model (DEM), this program calculates the incident solar radiation at each point during a particular day of the year. In addition to solar irradiance and atmospheric transmittance, the program takes into account the position of the Sun in user-defined time limits (one hour, for example), the incidence angles, the projected shadows and the distance from the Earth to the Sun.</ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Program for computing the solar radiation during one day"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:Given a digital elevation model (DEM), this program calculates the incident solar radiation at each point during a particular day of the year. In addition to solar irradiance and atmospheric transmittance, the program takes into account the position of the Sun in user-defined time limits (one hour, for example), the incidence angles, the projected shadows and the distance from the Earth to the Sun."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>MDE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Digital elevation model</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Digital elevation model in IMG raster format</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param01"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:DEM"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>directori_ombra</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Shadow directory</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[Directory where the different models derived from the DEM generated with <a href="Ombra.htm">Ombra</a> module have been saved. It is necessary to have a series of models that contain the range of possible azimuths that will occur during the chosen day. Within this range, representative ones will be generated (eg every 10 degrees) and must have their corresponding azimuth by name (...<i>110.img </i>, <i>120.img</i> ...). The program automatically determines (from the file names) the angular interval between available shadow layers (10 degrees in the example above). The minimum admissible interval is 1 degree (files ... 111.img, 112.img, 113.img, ...), but with intervals of the order of 10 degrees, sufficiently precise results are usually obtained]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param02"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:shadow_directory"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#anyURI">anyURI</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>dia</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Day</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Day for which the solar radiation calculation is carried out</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param04"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:day"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>7</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>8</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>9</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>10</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>11</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>12</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>13</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>14</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>15</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>16</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>17</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>18</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>19</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>20</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>21</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>22</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>23</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>24</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>25</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>26</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>27</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>28</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>29</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>30</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>31</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>mes</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Month</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Month for which the solar radiation calculation is carried out</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param05"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:month"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>7</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>8</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>9</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>10</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>11</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>12</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>any</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Year</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Year for which the solar radiation calculation is carried out</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param06"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:year"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>irradiancia_exoatm</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Exoatmospheric irradiance</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Estimated value of solar irradiance that reaches the outside of the Earth's atmosphere; 1366 is suggested</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param07"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:exoatmospheric_irradiance"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>tau</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Constant of extinction</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Constant of extinction; 0.288 is suggested</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param08"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:tau"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>increment_horari</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Hourly increase</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Increase in hourly units that is applied to the new solar position from the starting position and successively, to determine a new instantaneous calculation of potential radiation that represents the defined interval on average. It is positive from noon to sunset, or negative from noon to sunrise. By default, 1 is suggested</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param09"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:hourly_increase"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>tau_0_dia_clar</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>tau_0_dia_clar</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>It allows a more reasonable diffuse radiation calculation. 0.223 can be used for an exceptionally clear atmosphere, or 0.288 for an average forest clear atmosphere (Rothermel et al. 1986)</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param10"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:tau_0_dia_clar"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>percent_difus</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Percentage of diffuse vs direct radiation</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Percentage of diffuse radiation with respect to direct radiation with tau_0_day_clear. It can be a constant value for the entire raster, or be read from a raster specified in the /PERC_DIF_VS_DIRECT= parameter. Typically a value of 20 for 20% can be used.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param11"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:percent_difus"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>INSTANT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Instantaneous Calculation</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Restricts the calculation, which by default is daily accumulated, to only an instantaneous calculation. The value must be indicated as local solar time.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#time">time</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>INICI</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Start interval</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Allow defining a time interval (within the specified day) for the accumulated calculation of solar radiation. Values are reported as local solar time.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#time">time</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FINAL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>End interval</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Allow defining a time interval (within the specified day) for the accumulated calculation of solar radiation. Values are reported as local solar time.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#time">time</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>IRRAD_SPECTRAL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Spectral irradiance</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[Indicates that the solar irradiance provided is spectral and therefore the units of the output raster will be documented in 10 kJ / (m<sup>2</sup>·µm). If not specified, the units of the output raster will be documented in 10 kJ/m<sup>2</sup>.]]></ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TAU_0</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>TAU_0</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[It is allowed, through the optional parameter /TAU_0=, that TAU_0 be a specific value for each cell of the MDE (for example from atmospheric remote sensing data). In this case, /TAU_0= will indicate where is the raster that contains the values of TAU_0 in each cell; for example /TAU_0=c:\RadSolar\TAU_0_10-maig.img. This raster contains 4-byte real values and will have the same SRH and dimensions as the MDE; <a href="CanviPrj.htm">CanviPrj</a> and/or <a href="AdapRas.htm">AdapRas</a> can be used if needed. When the /TAU_0= parameter is specified the program ignores the eighth parameter of the command line (which is a general TAU_0 value for the entire raster); in this case it is suggested to indicate, for neatness, a value of -1 in the eighth parameter.]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input>
				<ows:Identifier>PERC_DIF_VS_DIRECT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>PERC_DIF_VS_DIRECT</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[It is allowed, through the optional parameter /PERC_DIF_VS_DIRECT=, that the percentage of diffuse radiation in relation to direct radiation be a specific value for each cell of the MDE (for example by interpolating data from solar radiation ground stations). In this case, /PERC_DIF_VS_DIRECT= will indicate where is the raster that contains the percentage values in each cell; for example /PERC_DIF_VS_DIRECT=c:\RadSolar\Perc_difusa_vs_directa.img. This raster contains 4-byte real values and will have the same SRH and dimensions as the MDE; <a href="CanviPrj.htm">CanviPrj</a> and/or <a href="AdapRas.htm">AdapRas</a> can be used if needed. When the /PERC_DIF_VS_DIRECT= parameter is specified, the program ignores the eleventh parameter of the command line (which is a general percentage value for the entire raster); in this case it is suggested to indicate, for neatness, a value of -1 in the eleventh parameter. Raster values are expressed as a percentage.]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>fitxer_sortida</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Output file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>IMG raster result of solar radiation calculation</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param03"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:output_file"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>